# gen_fu_l41_bus_latch_instant.log -- TDD red/green and MUT-LATCHNEG1 for the slave driver's request-capture instant
# Produced 2026-09-05T05:00:04Z on soc-l-11 from a detached archive of
# 218e9f3, this landing's files applied. The test needs no RTL and no core: it is the driver, one bus
# interface, the bridge register block and the memory model.
#
# WHAT IS CLAIMED: a request is captured at the ACCEPTING RISING EDGE, where req and gnt are both sampled
# high, for every grant-delay shape. NOT CLAIMED HERE: any statement about the core, whose bus behaviour
# rtl-arch recorded separately as a design property; and no stimulus-shape reproducer was built.
#
# THE SHAPE, which is the order-548 wave's: the core presents 0x80000348 at a rising edge, the driver grants at
# the falling edge, another driver writes a DUT input at that same falling edge and the combinational bus
# address settles to 0x80000340 before the accepting rising edge. The word answered must be 0x80000340's. A
# driver reading at the falling edge answers 0x80000348's word, a value the core never presented at any clock
# edge. The test moves the address in that half cycle by writing it one time unit after the falling edge at
# which gnt is observed, so the outcome does not depend on delta ordering between two processes.
#
# COMPILE (from the archive root), for each build below:
#   vcs -full64 -sverilog -ntb_opts uvm-1.2 +define+UVM +define+UVM_REGEX_NO_DPI -timescale=1ns/10ps -licqueue \
#       -f dv/auto_dv/tb/unit/gen_ut_bus_latch.f -top gen_ut_bus_latch_top -o <out>/simv -l <out>/compile.log
# RUN: ./simv +UVM_NO_RELNOTES ; excerpt FILTER for every run below:
#   grep -E '^(OK|FAIL)|gen_ut_bus_latch(_ablated)?: |GEN_UT_BUS_LATCH' <out>/stdout.log
#
# WHICH gen_agents_pkg.sv EACH BUILD CARRIES (sha256 first 16; nothing else differs between them):
#   RED       217c3910142dd3a0  exactly as committed at 218e9f3
#   GREEN     the same file with the capture moved to the accepting edge, and nothing else
#   MUTANT    7926d147db045acc  this landing's file (both fixes) with MUT-LATCHNEG1 injected
#   The landing's own file, which the GREEN pair below is the evidence for, is
#   7f9e7d6cb8b6efa2. The ack fix in it is not exercised by this
#   test, which never calls ack_seen; the RED/GREEN pair differs by the capture instant alone.

