# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MUTATION RECORD
#   id: MUT-LATCHNEG1
#   file:line: dv/auto_dv/env/gen_agents_pkg.sv, the request capture inside gen_bus_driver's grant branch
#   original: @(posedge vif.clk); p.addr = vif.addr; p.we = req_we(); p.be = req_be();
#   mutated:  p.addr = vif.addr; p.we = req_we(); p.be = req_be();   (read at the falling edge, no wait)
#   expected detector: the two moved-address checks of gen_ut_bus_latch
#   caught: the named test FAILS on both of them under the mutation
#   ablation control: the same mutant build with those two checks removed from a scratch copy of the test
#     PASSES, so nothing else in the test catches the mutation and the verdict belongs to the named checks
#   mutant diff: dv/auto_dv/evidence/gen_tdd_logs/mutations/gen_fu_l41_MUTLATCHNEG1_mutant.diff
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE FIX MOVES THE VALUE AND NOT THE TIME: the grant decision, gnt itself, the grant counters, gnt_delay,
# cycle_req, cycle_gnt, outstanding_at_gnt, stamp_gnt and the export cycle base are all taken at the granting
# falling edge, before the wait. Only addr, we, be and wdata, and the memory operation that uses them, moved.
#
# WHOLE-TB REGRESSION with this fix and the ack fix together, build outF from the same archive
# (dv/auto_dv/tb/gen_tb_local.sh), verdicts from the flow's own gen_verdict.decide:
#   ackgreen   verdict:  UVM_ERRORs 0
#   irqlines   verdict:  UVM_ERRORs 0
#   boot       verdict:  UVM_ERRORs 0
#   lockstorm  verdict:  UVM_ERRORs 0
#   ackgreen is gen_ut_irq_ack (the ack landing's red, green here), irqlines gen_ut_irq, boot gen_ut_boot,
#   lockstorm gen_ut_lockstep under a storm irq regime. All four PASS with zero UVM errors.
#
# AUDIT of every other clock-edge user in the env, for the register row:
#   gen_bus_driver serves BOTH buses through cfg.is_data, so this one change covers instruction and data.
#   Readers of DUT outputs already sample at the posedge: gen_rvfi_monitor (gen_rvfi_pkg.sv:136), the irq pin
#   sampler and the misc monitor (gen_checkers_pkg.sv:241 and :476), the coverage class's reset watcher
#   (gen_fcov_pkg.sv:1594).
#   The other four negedge processes drive inputs and read no combinational DUT output for a value:
#   gen_scrkey_driver (:453) reads ic_scr_key_req_o, whose only use is to start a delay count, not to produce
#   a returned value; gen_irq_driver (:629) and gen_dbg_driver (:713) read bridge fields written by the
#   scoreboard, not DUT pins; gen_ctrl_driver (:781) drives only.
